  "finalBehavior": [
    "A new Windows guard process may use45000ms only for its explicitly opted-in first acquire. Production withHermesHome is the opted-in caller.",
    "An existing AsyncLocalStorage guard session ignores nested startup options. Later ordinary acquire/release requests and unrelated first acquisitions retain15000ms.",
    "Metadata-import requests retain120000ms, including their existing larger bounded manifest limits.",
    "The PowerShell script, path identity/grant predicates, response schema/ID validation, onLoss behavior, namespace pins and release/owned process cleanup are unchanged. Linux behavior is unchanged.",
    "Cancellation during initial acquisition still waits for the reply or bounded failure, then active(signal) rejects before invoking the action. The dedicated allowance can lengthen this wait; immediate cancellation is not claimed.",
    "The existing desktop backend startup deadline remains60000ms. The change does not guarantee every future cold start fits; failure remains closed and requires actual Windows validation."
  ],
